The crew only comes back if its creatures had +1/+1 counters when they died and Marchesa saw those deaths. Establish a sacrifice outlet and a reliable counter source before committing to a big theft turn.

This is a mixed fictional street-crew and heist theme: eight cards keep their original Magic or official crossover characters, and the other 57 nonland cards have custom GTA character assignments below. Every custom art brief explicitly includes a visible character, even for mana rocks and spells. Lands are exempt.
The import file keeps the real Magic card names and rules. The casting sheet is a complete reskin plan, not rendered proxy artwork; the catalog currently displays the original card images. Custom nicknames and pictures do not change colors, types, abilities, mana values, names used by game rules or commander identity. Token rules also stay unchanged.

# CJ leads the crew
Marchesa, the Black Rose :: Custom character: CJ. Display nickname: CJ, Grove Street Boss. Art: CJ rallying the crew outside his neighborhood home. Dethrone supplies counters when you attack a player tied for highest life; a creature with a counter that dies under your control returns at the next end step, even if you do not own it.

# The original underworld cast
Professional Face-Breaker :: Original Magic character: New Capenna's professional enforcer. Keep a character-focused original printing; combat connections produce Treasure and Treasure becomes impulsive card access.
Grim Hireling :: Original Magic character: the hired rogue. Keep its character art; connecting with several players funds future turns and its Treasure-powered removal.
Body Launderer :: Original Magic character: New Capenna's underworld cleaner. Its connive counters and death-trigger recursion support the crew's repeated returns.
Body Dropper :: Original Magic character: New Capenna's enforcer. Sacrificing other creatures grows it, and its paid sacrifice ability supplies an additional outlet.
Dack Fayden :: Original Magic character: Dack himself, the thief. His artifact theft and looting fit both the character theme and the resource-stealing plan.
Black Cat, Cunning Thief :: Official crossover character: Felicia Hardy. Keep Black Cat's own artwork; each real entrance gives access to two cards from an opponent's top nine.
Satoru, the Infiltrator :: Original Magic character: Satoru, the infiltrator. Keep his own artwork; Marchesa's returning creatures become fresh cards.
Fain, the Broker :: Original Magic character: Fain, the dealmaker. He converts crew members into counters, counters into Treasure, or artifacts into an evasive token.

